# S15 Cognitive-Map Figure Provenance

Slide: S15, "Two systems, same data".

## Source

Stier et al. 2016, *Conservation Letters*, "Integrating Expert Perceptions
into Food Web Conservation and Management".

Local source PDF:
`talk-usuk-forum-2026/Reference_Papers/Stier_2016_ExpertPerceptionsFoodWeb.pdf`
(PDFs under `talk-usuk-forum-2026/` are intentionally gitignored).

## Talk Claim

The slide can safely say:

- The study elicited fuzzy cognitive maps from 27 Northeast Pacific herring
  experts.
- Expert food-web perceptions separated into two structural groups.
- Under simulated herring recovery, those groups gave different ecosystem
  response expectations.
- Background, experience, and affiliation did not explain the split cleanly.

Do not overstate this as a measured social tipping point. It is evidence that
the same ecological data are interpreted through distinct knowledge structures,
which matters for governance under uncertainty.

